/// Absolute path to the asset configuration loaded at startup.
///
/// Resolved at configure time and baked in, so it never depends on the process
/// working directory. The tradeoff is that a binary built here expects the
/// repository at the same absolute path; a shipped game will need this resolved
/// at runtime instead. Override with -DENGINE_ASSETS_CONFIG=<path>.
inline constexpr char kAssetsConfig[] = "@ENGINE_ASSETS_CONFIG@";

/// Absolute path to the level file the game loads at startup.
///
/// The same configure-time tradeoff as [kAssetsConfig], and for the same reason: a
/// binary built here expects the repository at the same absolute path. Override with
/// -DENGINE_LEVEL_FILE=<path>.
inline constexpr char kLevelFile[] = "@ENGINE_LEVEL_FILE@";

/// How tall the game's world is, in 64-pixel grid cells.
///
/// The level format carries no height field - a [engine::level::LevelGrid] takes it
/// as an argument precisely because the level file is not entitled to say how tall
/// the world it drops into is - so the world height is a decision this game makes,
/// and it belongs next to the level path rather than inside the level loader.
/// Override with -DENGINE_LEVEL_CELLS_TALL=<n>.
///
/// An integer rather than a float, because a count of cells is whole: there is no
/// such thing as half a grid cell, and a half-cell would be a request the loader
/// could only round, which is the rounding this engine refused when it decided that
/// a frame count must divide a texture width exactly. The scene converts once, at
/// the call to `withCellsTall`, which is the only place the two types meet.
inline constexpr unsigned int kLevelCellsTall = @ENGINE_LEVEL_CELLS_TALL@u;

